00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.800
- At the same time newsroom shrank,

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.117
and the 24-hour news cycle emerged.

00:05:34.117 --> 00:05:36.270
"The need to produce
greater quantities of news

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.737
at a faster pace," according
to scholar, David A. Logan,

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:42.240
"incentivize journalists to
get the news first and fast

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.100
rather than first and right."

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.620
Misinformation, unsurprisingly followed.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:49.470
For example, in 1985, the
Soviet Union started a rumor

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.440
that AIDS had been created
in a us military laboratory.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:53.970
This spread like wildfire

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:56.370
and by 1987, reporter Dan Rather,

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.710
repeated the accusations on CBS

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.470
without asking the
government for a response.

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:04.920
By the time the internet rolled
around, all bets were off.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.630
If the printing press lowered the barrier

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.890
to spread information,

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:09.690
the internet obliterated it.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:11.820
But the digital web of misinformation

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.260
was far less mainstream.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.187
As scholar, Dave Karp, writes,

00:06:15.187 --> 00:06:17.910
"Conspiratorial websites in the mid 1990s

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.790
