00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:01.860
So where does all of this leave us?

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.867
As Stanford scholar
Renee DiResta explains,

00:16:04.867 --> 00:16:07.860
"We are living in an
epistemological take-down

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.440
wherein people think facts
don't exist anymore."

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:13.680
And that feels like a pretty
daunting problem to have.

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.660
But this isn't the first
time humans have grappled

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.940
with concerns about the
extinction of truth.

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:20.190
A key question asked by
some of the philosophers

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:22.350
associated with postmodernism

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:25.530
was whether or not truth
was still a useful category.

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:27.750
Now, this is in contrast
to ancient philosophers,

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:29.190
like Plato and Aristotle,

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:31.440
and some more modern
idealists, like Kant Hegle,

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:32.460
who in their own ways

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.410
all believed that human reason

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:36.570
could arrive at some understanding

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:39.180
of universal truths and concepts.

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:41.520
But for philosophers like Jacque Derrida

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:42.750
and Emmanuel Levinas,

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.240
who drew inspiration from
19th century thinkers

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:46.470
like Nietzche and Kierkegaard,

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:48.840
classically metaphysical models of truth

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:52.230
sort of flatten the realities
of actual human existence

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:54.750
and often favor a more theological

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.550
or hierarchical way of thinking.

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:59.280
Now, according to philosopher
Jean-Francois Lyotard,

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:00.600
post-modernism is defined

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:03.420
by an incredulity towards metanarratives.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:04.500
Now, in other words,

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.450
post-modernism is a sensibility

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:08.400
which is skeptical of metaphysical

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:09.930
or scientific modes of thinking

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:13.710
which claim to explain everything
in one consistent system,

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:15.600
i.e., that all existence

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:20.600
is oriented towards one cosmic
omnipotent being or concept.

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:21.930
Now, Derrida thought

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:25.350
that instead of some
universal hierarchical truth,

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:28.500
meaning has more to do with close readings

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:32.190
that reckon with a fundamental
difference or undecidability

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.050
in all texts and situations.

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:36.420
For some, this seems like an admittance

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:38.070
that truth doesn't exist

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.990
and everything is ultimately subjective,

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:43.680
while for others this is a
position of epistemic humility.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:46.410
Now for Derrida, this meant
that the notions of truth

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:49.200
that underlie various
colonial political projects

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:52.260
were no longer to be taken
as universally valid,

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:55.050
which too many would be very, very good.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.160
But for others,

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:58.830
making truth supposedly subjective

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:01.530
could have the cultural effect
of creating a free-for-all

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:04.890
in which all ideas of truth
and justice are equally valid.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.990
And philosophers like Alain Badiou

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:09.540
have noted how this free
market approach to truth

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:11.640
has been a wonderful gift for capitalism

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:13.800
as it takes traditional
categories of truth,

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.840
like art, love, science,

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:17.460
and turns them into things

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:19.890
that can be more easily
marketed, bought, or sold.

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:23.040
So art becomes culture.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.300
Love becomes sex.

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:25.980
Science becomes technology.

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:28.680
For example scientific
innovation and discovery

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:29.850
used to be motivated

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:33.840
by a desire to better understand
ourselves and the cosmos.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.510
But technology became about using science

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:39.780
to build fancy gizmos that
makes stockholders happy.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:43.380
And while love was once about
authentic romantic connection,

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:46.620
now dating apps and websites call our data

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:48.390
while teaching us to reduce the complexity

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:49.830
of love and sexuality

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:52.260
to a few doctored images on our phones.

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:54.060
In mine, I have lots of hair.

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:56.490
Things that once gave meaning to our lives

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:57.930
now become mere products.

00:18:57.930 --> 00:19:00.510
For Badiou, the reintroduction of truth

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:02.670
is necessary to combat this.

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:06.480
But rather than the singular
truth of Plato or religion,

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:08.310
he argues for truths

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:10.740
which are relative to specific situations.

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:14.040
And these truths are what
can give meaning to our lives

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.840
outside of the free market,

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:18.900
whether that truth is a
lover, a commitment to art,

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:21.510
a passion for science,
or a desire for justice.

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:22.357
And in case you're thinking,

00:19:22.357 --> 00:19:24.960
"Yeah, but what if my truth is fascism?"

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:27.540
Badiou argues that the thing
that all truths have in common

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:28.860
is a principle of equality.

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:31.140
So I guess your fascist streams

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.640
will have to remain just that.

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:35.370
But in the absence of
such high-minded ideals,

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:37.470
we're left in the ruthless ruins

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.960
that post-modern capitalism has rot

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:41.520
and that makes it really easy

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:44.520
for misinformation to
infiltrate the discourse,

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:45.720
which is one thing

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:48.180
if you decide to become
a quirky flat Earther,

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:50.310
